 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "How do you get a fleet past a chain?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "You carry it over a hill. This is Istanbul, and in April 1453 it was still Constantinople."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Who held it then?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "April 1453",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Only the Byzantines, inside their walls. The Ottomans held almost everything around it."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "And a great chain across the Golden Horn kept the Ottoman fleet out of the harbour.",
   "scene": "chain",
   "date": "April 1453",
   "place": "Golden Horn"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So the fleet was stuck outside?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Right. On the twentieth of April, four Christian ships even fought their way past it and into the harbour."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So what did Mehmed do?",
   "scene": "overland",
   "date": "22 April 1453",
   "place": "Galata"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "He moved his ships over land. His men laid a track of greased logs over the hill behind Galata."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "And they hauled about seventy ships up the slope and down into the Golden Horn, behind the chain."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Did the defenders see it coming?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Not exactly. One morning, Ottoman ships were simply inside their harbour. Now the walls along the water needed defenders too."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "When did the city fall?",
   "scene": "fall",
   "date": "29 May 1453",
   "place": "Constantinople",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.4,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.45,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "On the twenty-ninth of May, 1453. Before dawn, Mehmed sent wave after wave against the land walls."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The Genoese commander Giustiniani was badly wounded and carried away, and the defence began to break."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Emperor Constantine the Eleventh died in the fighting. He was the last Byzantine emperor.",
   "scene": "constantine",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.6,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.62,
     0.42,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "That day, Mehmed rode into the city.",
   "scene": "entry",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.55,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.2
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "He went to Hagia Sophia, and turned the great church into a mosque.",
   "scene": "hagia",
   "date": "",
   "place": "Hagia Sophia",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.55,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.62,
     0.4,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And the city became the Ottoman capital?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1453",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Right. For more than four hundred and sixty years, until 1922."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: Selim the Grim, and eight years that changed the map. Like the video and follow History Sketches.",
   "scene": "zonaro",
